# .cursor/rules

These are project rules for the Cursor agent when editing this repo.

## 1) Stack and scope

* App is React with TypeScript and Tailwind CSS.
* Use Vite or Next.js app router only if an existing project already uses it. Do not migrate build tools without an explicit task.
* Keep changes minimal and scoped to the described task.

## 2) Code style

* Follow TypeScript strict mode. Always type function inputs and outputs. Prefer zod or type guards near API boundaries.
* Prefer composition over inheritance. Use small pure functions.
* Use named exports. Default export only for React components in `app` or `pages`.
* Use Prettier defaults. Avoid long lines > 100 chars.
* No magic numbers. Lift constants to `const` at top of file.

## 3) React patterns

* Function components with hooks. No class components.
* State rules: local UI state with `useState` or `useReducer`. Server cache or async data with React Query if already installed. If not installed, use `fetch` with SWR-like patterns.
* Side effects in `useEffect` with cleanups. Avoid redundant effects.
* Memoization: use `useMemo` and `useCallback` only for expensive work or stable deps.
* Props should be minimal and typed. Prefer `Props` interfaces. Example:

  ```ts
  interface ButtonProps {
    children: React.ReactNode;
    variant?: "primary" | "secondary";
    onClick?: () => void;
  }
  ```

## 4) Tailwind usage

* Prefer utility classes. Extract to components via `cn` helper when class lists get long.
* Use semantic spacing and sizing. Avoid arbitrary values unless necessary.
* Do not inline hex colors. Use theme tokens. Add new tokens in `tailwind.config.js` under `theme.extend`.
* Responsive first. Add `sm`, `md`, `lg`, `xl` variants as needed.

## 5) File structure

* `src/components/` for reusable components. Each component in its own folder with `index.tsx` and `index.test.tsx` if tests exist.
* `src/pages` or `src/app` for routes depending on framework. Do not mix both.
* `src/lib/` for utilities, hooks, and constants. Split by feature.
* `src/types/` for shared TypeScript types.

## 6) Accessibility

* All interactive elements must be reachable by keyboard and have `aria-*` where needed.
* Buttons are `<button>`, not clickable `<div>`.
* Images need `alt` text. Decorative images use `alt=""`.

## 7) Testing

* Create tests for new pure utilities and complex hooks. Light smoke tests for components that render logic branches.
* Use Testing Library with jest or vitest. No shallow rendering.

## 8) API and data

* Do not change server contracts. Create TypeScript types that mirror API responses and narrow them in the client.
* Validate unsafe inputs. Add minimal error states and loading states to all async UIs.

## 9) Performance

* Avoid unnecessary re-renders. Derive state instead of duplicating it.
* Code split large routes and heavy components.
* Use `React.Suspense` boundaries where helpful.

## 10) Git hygiene

* Small, focused commits with imperative messages. Example: "Add Card component with hover state".
* If Cursor plans to touch many files, propose a plan in a comment at the top of the PR and get approval.

## 11) Comments and docs

* Write a short JSDoc for exported functions and complex hooks.
* Add usage examples in component folders when needed.

## 12) Tailwind design tokens

* Primary color is `primary` from theme. Use `bg-primary`, `text-primary`, and `hover:bg-primary/90`.
* Spacing uses multiples of 2 or 4. Typography uses Tailwind defaults plus any tokens defined in the theme.

## 13) Linting and formatting

* Fix all TypeScript and ESLint errors before committing. Prefer autofixes.
* Run typecheck before pushing.

## 14) Component template

Use this when creating a new component.

```tsx
import * as React from "react";
import { cn } from "@/lib/cn";

interface Props {
  className?: string;
  children?: React.ReactNode;
}

export function Card({ className, children }: Props) {
  return (
    <div className={cn("rounded-2xl shadow p-4 bg-white", className)}>
      {children}
    </div>
  );
}
```

## 15) Do not

* Do not add new dependencies without a clear reason and changelog entry.
* Do not refactor unrelated files during feature work.
* Do not weaken TypeScript types to `any` or `unknown` without comments.

## 16) Pull request checklist

* Types pass. Lint passes. Build succeeds. Tests updated.
* Added empty state, loading state, and error state where applicable.
* Verified responsive layout at 360, 768, 1024 widths.

## 17) Tailwind class ordering

* Use logical order: layout, box model, spacing, typography, visuals, interactivity, responsive variants.
* Example: `flex items-center justify-between p-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 bg-white rounded-xl shadow hover:shadow-md md:p-6`.

## 18) Env and config

* Do not hardcode URLs or keys. Read from `import.meta.env` or `process.env` depending on toolchain.
* Provide safe fallbacks and guard against `undefined`.

## 19) Internationalization

* If i18n is present, wrap user strings with the translation function. Do not introduce new hardcoded copy.

## 20) How Cursor should operate

* Before large edits, outline the approach as comments at top of the changed file.
* When unsure, prefer creating a new component or utility rather than changing shared ones.
* Keep PRs small. If a change spans more than 300 lines, propose splitting.
